  I read the README and listed the workspace crates, but the comment with the
  summary may not have been posted. I made no code changes.

  The first `wf comment` call failed because `--done` requires `--step`. I then
  ran `wf work submit`, which succeeded (`submitted #qp7jzs`). When I retried
  the comment, the worktree had already been deleted, so I don't know whether it
  posted. I didn't retry from outside the worktree, since `wf` needs the repo.

  The summary I tried to post:

  - **`wf-core`:** pure domain logic (events, item model, lifecycle and briefs)
  with no IO.
  - **`wf-store`:** the event-log store.
  - **`wf-net`:** sync protocols over iroh, written against generic streams and
  a `SyncLog` trait.
  - **`wf-daemon`:** owns the store while it runs, runs sessions and merges
  approved work.
  - **`wf-harness`:** runs agents over ACP.
  - **`wf-vcs`:** the only crate that runs `git`.
  - **`wf-cli`:** the `wf` binary, which goes through `Workspace`.

  The README covers milestones M0–M2:
  - the signed event log
  - sync between machines
  - agent sessions in worktrees with review and merge
  - the permission-request decider chain

  Check item #qp7jzs for the comment. If it's missing, the text above is what it
  should say.

